n i speak with my tutor as  you're going to see when i do my exit  video with my tutor  next week and we might even make that a  live stream or at any rate i will uh you  know make a video which will be  available  on youtube  however i do have 19 000 passively known  words but i have 57 000 links words that  i have words and phrases that i have  saved  so i really know a small subset  of all the words that i have saved  i know a third of them  so there's two thirds that i've met  looked up and no longer know what they  mean  uh so i i wanted to do a little more  analysis of this  so what i did was uh i sort of went into  the vocab section  and  there uh you know you initially you look  at  if you look at the status it has every  one of the four or the five statuses  are ticked off so the total number of  vocabulary that i have saved the total  number of my  created links  is 57 56 970. okay  now  i can go and change the parameters  so let's for example say that i go into  my a vocab section  and i choose only status one so i tick  the others i get rid of the others i'm  only going to look at status one words  well it shows me here  that 36  500 of my 57 000 saved links i hope i'm  not confusing you  but the bulk of the words that i have  met and looked up in a dictionary are  still status one in other words  new so  those are words that haven't shown up  again  or i don't remember them or whatever  so  so i went into my status one words  and found that actually where there were  a lot of words there that i actually  knew or i had some familiarity with so i  went into my list and started upgrading  them to status 2 or status 3 or even  known  now that's not a tremendously useful  thing to do in a way  because if our if there are words there  that i know  and if they show up again you know i  have an opportunity while i'm in the  lesson page  to upgrade them to move them to status 2  or status 3 or make them known so to do  this you know in a concentrated fashion  in